// Japanese era years (nengō, wareki): 令和8年 is 2026. Every Japanese
// government form, many contracts and some file formats date by era.
//
// An era is proclaimed, not computed, so the table is ICU's: all 237 eras
// since Taika in 645, each with its first day and its English name as ICU
// gives it ("Reiwa", "Heisei", older ones with their years, "Taika
// (645–650)"). The year of an era counts from 1 in the calendar year the
// era began; months and days are Gregorian, and Julian before 15 October
// 1582, as ICU's are. Dates before Taika are given in Taika with years of
// 0 and less.
import buddhistcal

